      "summary": "Tipula furca (Common Crane Fly) is a native, well-distributed species recorded from Florida. Species-level biology is very thinly documented; most fields draw on well-sourced Tipula / Tipulidae genus-level data from UF/IFAS and peer-reviewed sources, with T. furca-specific facts (appearance, size, Florida record) confirmed from Minnesota Seasons, EOL, and the iNaturalist Florida crane fly checklist. Overall confidence is moderate-high for genus-level ecology fields and lower for species-specific seasonality and habitat detail.",
